WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.801
-Thank you so much
for coming here in person.

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.271
-It's so fun to be here.
It's so nice to see you, pally.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.106
-It's so nice
to see your face, buddy.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.609
Thank you.
We talked during the quarantine,

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:12.612
obviously, and you helped me out
with some bits.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.147
You sent me a couple photos

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.448
from quarantine
that I wanted to show.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.449
-Mm-hmm.
-This first one here,

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:20.320
I just wanted --
Who is this,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.722
and what exactly is going --
-This who I am now, Jimmy.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.757
-Is that the new you?
-This is the new me.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.193
This is actually a picture of --
That outfit is from

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.963
the "Tonight Show" aunties bit
that we did.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.731
-I love that.
-I was at home wearing it

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.299
that day
because I was very excited,

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:38.705
because that is the first car
I have ever owned in my life.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.306
-What?
-I got my first car

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.741
during quarantine.
-Wow!

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.576
-Thank you.
-Wait. This is --

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.111
This is major.
You never bought a car.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:48.380
-Yeah, 'cause I'm a big, like,
subway, bus...bitch.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.716
And --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:55.088
I'm such a bitch.
Trolley...

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.956
And so, yeah,
I never used to drive.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.791
I always had a license
that I never used,

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:02.195
and then, during quarantine,
when I didn't like --

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.796
The subway wasn't open.
I was just, like,

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.732
"I want to have some agency,"
and so I wanted to go

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:09.034
look for cars,
and my husband was like,

00:01:09.034 --> 00:01:11.537
"Maybe get, like, a Mini Cooper
or, like, a fun car

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:15.241
or, like, a Jeep or a BMW,"
and I was like, "No.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.408
I know what I want."

00:01:16.408 --> 00:01:19.345
And it's a white
Subaru Forester.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.013
And, um --
-I've never even heard

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.581
of a Subaru Forester.
-It's so basic.

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:24.016
I'm like, "Mwah, mwah, mwah!
It's basic."

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.252
-Oh, my God!
-And my -- It's funny,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.322
'cause Alice is 15 now.
My older daughter's 15,

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.756
and she --
-Wow. Is she 15?

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:32.625
-I think she's looking
at that car, knowing, like,

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.528
that's the car she's gonna learn
to drive on, and she's like...

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.063
She was really pushing for,
like, a cuter, cooler car,

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:39.299
and I was like,
"No, I want a car

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.167
that looks like
a medical sneaker."

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.102
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.505
"It's so safe.
It looks like

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.573
Judah Friedlander's
frickin' sneakers.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:51.443
And she's like, "But, Mom,
that's such a Karen car."

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:53.813
And I was like,
"I'm naming her Karen,"

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.115
and now I'm always, like,
"Should we take Karen

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:59.519
to the store?"
and no one in the family

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:02.154
finds it humorous
that I named the car.

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:04.057
-Did you --
Did you take Karen

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.791
and get out of the city at all
during quarantine?

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:08.460
-Yeah, we did.
After about...

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.195
'Cause we were in the city
in the beginning,

00:02:10.195 --> 00:02:12.098
'cause I remember I was talking
to you in the beginning,

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.565
and you were like, "Do you
want to come to our house?"

00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:14.867
Like, you were concerned for me

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.802
that we were just in the
apartment for a couple months.

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:20.206
But, like, so many New Yorkers,
my kids, at a certain point,

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.741
hadn't been outside
in six or eight weeks.

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:25.845
They were becoming like the
children in the "Secret Garden."

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.113
Like, "May I have some...?"

00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:29.515
-"Is that sunlight, Mum?"

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.517
-"I would like
to meet the wind."

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:32.785
[ Laughter ]
And so...

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.286
-"No, you can't meet the wind,
not today."

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:36.322
"Not today."
So, after, like,

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.157
a couple months, we did --
we were fortunate enough --

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:40.092
we rented a house
outside the city.

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:42.428
And the first time we got to
this place, where it had a yard

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:45.331
and we could go outside --
I was, like,

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.466
outside in the morning with my
coffee without a whole protocol

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:51.337
in my own little yard,
and the first morning

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.372
that we were there,
I was standing outside,

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:55.374
and we were looking down --
You can see the Hudson River

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:56.976
from where we are.
It's so pretty.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.711
And I heard -- I'm standing
there with my coffee,

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:02.215
and I just hear
something going...

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:06.185
"Help! Help!"
And it -- I was like,

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:09.121
"Is that a 'help' or a bird?"

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:12.025
'Cause I've been in my house
for two months, right?

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.227
So I'm like, "Is that
a person saying 'help'?"

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.862
So, I went
and got my older daughter,

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.196
and I was like, "Come out here,
come out here."

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:20.066
And we're standing outside --
again, like, mole people.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.567
Haven't been outside.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.903
-Looking down at the river,
and we're waiting,

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.838
and, like, a couple minutes go
by, and then we hear it again.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.975
It was like, "Help! Help!"

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.943
So then I called Jeff out.
Like, he's from the country.

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:32.745
He grew up in the country.
He'll know if this is a bird.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.179
'Cause I'm thinking, like,
"We're gonna freak out

00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:36.182
about this and he's gonna be
like, 'Hey, you weirdo.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.683
It's a bird.'"
-Yes.

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:40.719
-So, he comes out.
We're all standing out there.

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:42.721
We hear it again --
"Help!"

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:44.590
So, we called the cops.
We're like, "What do we do?"

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.325
We called the cops.
Our first day out of the house,

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:49.529
we're, like, calling the cops at
the height of the pandemic.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:52.732
Cop comes, he listens.
And, of course, he's like,

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.734
"Well, hello!"
Like, he's got a strong voice.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.702
'Cause I've just been like,
"Everybody okay?"

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:58.137
Like, I can't --
-Yeah, sure.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.605
And then we hear it again,
"Help!"

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:03.576
So, the cops take off.
And then, we found out, like,

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.279
a couple hours later
that it was a guy

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:09.682
who flipped a kayak
in the Hudson...

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.183
-Are you --
-...and was floating north

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:13.653
in the Hudson and just, like,
no oar and just was flo--

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:16.655
And they found him
like a mile north.

00:04:16.655 --> 00:04:19.959
-What is going --
Tina, you saved a man's life!

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.894
-I saved a man's life!
-Oh, my gosh!

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.862
Wait. What?!
-He doesn't know

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:26.265
that it was us, but...
-I can't believe

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.566
that happened to you.
-Isn't that crazy?

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:30.803
Also, never kayak!
Why?

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.139
-Oh, my gosh.
-Never kayak!

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.706
-"Never kayak."
-On the Hudson?

00:04:34.706 --> 00:04:38.177
That's not, like, a stream.
It's like a rat toilet.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.580
Why are you kayaking the Hudson?
-Oh, my God.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.649
That's the lesson learned.
I love that, of all people,

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:45.317
it would happen to you.
-Day one.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:47.186
-Day one, come out with
your coffee and you hear

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.655
someone screaming for help.
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.524
Oh, my gosh.
That is bizarre.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:53.659
You saved a man's life.
This is great.

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:56.062
-That's it.
-Well, let's talk about --

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:58.597
it's a good segue into "Soul."
-Yes.

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:01.534
About the value of life.
-The value of life.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.369
Gosh, I loved it.
Watched it over the weekend

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.237
with the kids.
You're phenomenal in this.

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:06.973
-Aww, thank you.
It's so beautiful.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:09.108
It's really a piece of art.
I mean, don't you think?

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.511
I mean, it's like --
You have the --

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:13.780
the beauty of the way New York
is rendered,

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.247
which I've never seen
an animation of New York

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:16.849
rendered so realistically
and beautifully.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.986
And then, also, this whole other
ethereal world

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.154
of The Great Before
and The Great Beyond.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:25.123
-Yeah.
-So, yeah, it's the story of --

00:05:25.123 --> 00:05:27.960
"Soul" is the story of
a guy named Joe Gardner

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.097
who is a middle-school
band teacher whose real goal

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.798
is to be a professional
jazz musician,

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:34.633
and he's kind of, like,
hung up on

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:36.369
making this happen for himself.

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:39.672
And then, something happens to
him that I won't give away,

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:42.474
and he is kind of
knocked out of his body,

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:46.011
and his soul goes up to
a place called The Great Before,

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:48.180
which is where souls come from.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.450
And he's trying
to get back to Earth and --

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.718
And he's just gotten
his big break.

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:53.986
He's trying
to get back to Earth.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:57.123
And he meets my character there,
which is a little --

00:05:57.123 --> 00:06:00.158
unctuous little soul named 22.
-22, man.

00:06:00.158 --> 00:06:04.597
-Who has never been convinced
to go down into Earth

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.498
and get into a body.
She's had all these mentors

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:08.467
try to explain to her,
like, why it would be great

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:10.502
to live on Earth,
and she's like, "I don't know.

00:06:10.502 --> 00:06:12.438
Sounds painful.
It sounds scary.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.839
I'm gonna pass."
She just wants to skip

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:15.173
the whole thing.
-Yeah.

00:06:15.173 --> 00:06:17.043
She doesn't get Earth.
She doesn't quite understand.

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.310
"I didn't really get it."
But whatever.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.612
-Yeah. So -- Yeah.
So, they have --

00:06:20.612 --> 00:06:22.881
You know, it's sort of a buddy
comedy between the two of them,

00:06:22.881 --> 00:06:24.683
and she's trying -- She's like,
"You can take my spot."

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:26.285
Like, "We'll help you
get back to Earth.

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:27.453
It's your body.
You can have it."

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.888
-It's phenomenal.
I don't want to tell anyone

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:30.956
what happens in the film
'cause it's just worth watching.

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:33.959
And it's beautiful the way it
unfolds, and you get to see it.

00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:35.093
But do you want
to set up this clip at all?

00:06:35.093 --> 00:06:37.029
-Oh, yeah!
So, this clip, I think, is --

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:41.634
So, Jamie's character, Joe,
is in The Great Before

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:45.037
with me, where all souls get
their personality traits

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:49.207
and what makes them unique.
And I take him to this place

00:06:49.207 --> 00:06:51.910
called The Hall of Everything,
which is a place where

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.613
new souls can try everything
on Earth -- every job,

00:06:54.613 --> 00:06:56.682
every hobby, every occup--
Everything.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.317
-"Maybe I like music.
Maybe I like cooking."

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:02.087
-Yeah, to see what sparks
life in them.

00:07:02.087 --> 00:07:03.756
And so, this is me
taking him around there.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:06.425
-Yeah. Here we go.
Let's take a look.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:09.361
-Where do you want to start?
-Come on.

00:07:09.361 --> 00:07:12.698
Croissants, cakes?
Baking could be your spark.

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:14.967
-Yeah!
But, um, I don't get it.

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:17.170
-Just smell it.
-Can't, and neither can you.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:18.704
-What?
You're right.

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:20.139
I can't smell.

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:22.575
We can't --
We can't taste, either?

00:07:22.575 --> 00:07:25.044
-All that stuff is in your body.

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:27.846
-No smell, no taste --
-Or touch.

00:07:27.846 --> 00:07:28.914
See?

00:07:28.914 --> 00:07:32.151
♪♪

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.520
-Okay! I get it.
Moving on.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.656
-[ Laughs ]
Tina Fey, everybody!

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:40.393
"Soul" premieres Christmas Day
on Disney+.

